    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0266" n="262" xml:id="pg262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/2096: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-09T15:00:00+08:00">February 9, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 9—2:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>97. Following from Hong Kong.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“February 2, 2 p.m. Numerous refugees desire to make claim for personal
                        losses sustained in China. Please advise as to form in which claim should be
                        made; also whether any fee should be collected.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>In view of lack of any details which might suggest some method of settling these
                    claims informally as is contemplated at Nanking, I see no alternative to the use
                    of the prescribed form of “application for the support of claims against foreign
                    governments” but I would appreciate the Department’s comments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
